quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  23,75,"Were We to show them mercy and remove whatever evil was upon them, they would surely persist, wandering confused in their rebellion."
  23,76,"We already overtook them with punishment, yet they were not submissive to their Lord, nor did they humble themselves (to receive His mercy)."
  23,77,"When We open a door of severe punishment upon them, behold, they will fall into utter despair."
  23,78,"He is the One Who made for you (your) ears, eyes and hearts. How seldom are you thankful!"
  23,79,"He is the One Who created you on the earth, and to Him shall you be gathered."
  23,80,He is the One Who gives life and causes death. And to Him belongs the alternation of the night and the day. Do you not then understand?
  23,81,But they say just like what the ancients said.
  23,82,"They say: ‘What, when we are dead and become dust and bones, shall we be resurrected?"
  23,83,"Surely, we have heard such promises, and (so did) our forefathers before. These are just the fairy tales of the ancients.’"
  23,84,"Say: ‘To whom does the earth belong and whoever is upon it, if you know?’"
  23,85,They will (promptly) say: ‘To Allah.’ Say: ‘Will you not then be mindful of advice?’
  23,86,Say: ‘Who is the Lord of the seven heavens and the Lord of the Great Throne?’
  23,87,They will (promptly) say: ‘To Allah.’ Say: ‘Will you not then be conscious of Him?’
  23,88,"Say: ‘In Whose Hand is the dominion of all things and Who provides shelter (to everything), and against Whom no shelter can be provided if you know?’"
  23,89,They will (promptly) say: ‘To Allah.’ Say: ‘How then are you deceived?
